# Apps read MTK vendor config props through the graphics and GPU stack: every app's
# RenderThread reads vendor_mtk_gpu_prop, and the media/display paths read others. The
# stock policy exposed these to apps through its mtk_core_property_type blanket, which
# LOS plat does not carry, so the reads now land on the vendor props marked
# vendor_public_property_type in property.te. Grant non-isolated app domains read on the
# public set (the "public" in vendor_public_property_type means app-readable). Without
# this every app's RenderThread is denied vendor_mtk_gpu_prop and the screen blanks under
# enforcing.
allow { appdomain -isolated_app -isolated_compute_app } vendor_public_property_type:file { getattr map open read };
